1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,199
Some ideas happen in order.

2
00:00:02,249 --> 00:00:04,874
First, price breaks out on heavy volume.

3
00:00:04,924 --> 00:00:07,741
Then, within a few days, the volume dries up.

4
00:00:08,204 --> 00:00:12,365
Add the Recent structure break Group, and the relative volume signal.

5
00:00:13,331 --> 00:00:15,039
Then add a THEN box.

6
00:00:15,089 --> 00:00:19,421
It has a First part, a Then part with a number of days, and an optional Cancel.

7
00:00:19,883 --> 00:00:21,804
First: an upward break,

8
00:00:21,854 --> 00:00:24,672
on at least one and a half times the usual volume.

9
00:00:31,034 --> 00:00:36,134
Then, within five daily closes: volume is back below one and a half times usual.

10
00:00:38,091 --> 00:00:40,695
The editor writes it out in plain words.

11
00:00:40,745 --> 00:00:44,842
First and Then on the same day don't count: Then has to come later.

12
00:00:45,293 --> 00:00:48,388
Save it, and run it on your coins at a past moment.

13
00:01:11,877 --> 00:01:14,438
Yes means both steps happened, in order.

14
00:01:14,488 --> 00:01:16,332
A No with a skip mark is part-way:

15
00:01:16,352 --> 00:01:19,887
the breakout happened, and the drop can still come in time.

16
00:01:20,353 --> 00:01:22,872
To see whether anything usually followed,

17
00:01:22,922 --> 00:01:25,440
open the Set and tap Study this Set.
